  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Loma Linda University 2026-2027 Catalog (effective Summer Quarter 2026) program page 'Physician Assistant - M.P.A.' (School of Allied Health Professions, Department of Physician Assistant Sciences). The catalog publishes the curriculum split by First Year (35 courses = 83 units) and Second Year (12 courses = 52 units); 83 + 52 = 135 = catalog Total Units 135. Second Year = eight six-week clinical rotations (each 6 units) covering family medicine, internal medicine, pediatrics, obstetrics/gynecology, general surgery, emergency medicine, behavioral medicine, plus one elective; plus Professional Issues and Capstone. Catalog notes: PAST 572 fulfills the service learning requirement. Normal time to complete: 2.33 years (eight academic quarters), full-time enrollment required. Prerequisite courses required before enrollment (human anatomy and physiology with lab; general chemistry sequence with lab or inorganic/organic/biochemistry sequence with labs; general microbiology with lab; general psychology; general sociology or cultural anthropology; college algebra; one-year English composition sequence; baccalaureate degree; 2,000 hours paid patient-care experience) are documented here and not placed in any term. The only per-course prerequisites stated in the catalog are PAST 502 (requires PAST 501) and PAST 503 (requires PAST 501, PAST 502); the remaining published order is the official sequence, so other prereq arrays are intentionally empty.",
